{"id": "135021", "revid": "235382", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=135021", "title": "St Asaph", "text": "St Asaph (Welsh: \"Llanelwy\") is one of Britain's smallest cities, having a population of only 3,355. It is located in the lower parts of the Vale of Clwyd, in north Wales. The city's cathedral is one of four in Wales.\nGet in.\nOn the A55 North Wales Expressway between Holywell and Abergele.\nClosest rail station is Rhyl from where the 54 bus [dead link] will take you to St Asaph."}
{"id": "135033", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=135033", "title": "Ponterwyd", "text": "Ponterwyd is a village in Ceredigion.\nGet in.\nIt is on the A44 about 20 km from Aberystwyth.\nThe 525-X47 [dead link] buses running between Aberystwyth and Llanidloes pass through Ponterwyd"}
